    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_2f0b0eb0",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: meme_image; hasOverallIntent: Mysogynous; overall-intent-description: The image depicts a woman with an exaggerated expression of shock and disbelief, holding her head in her hands. The text reads: \"If he's marrying me then why's he fucking a goat.\" This juxtaposition of a woman's emotional reaction with the crude, sexually explicit text targets women by mocking their perceived emotional instability and irrationality in the face of betrayal or infidelity. The meme relies on the stereotype that women are 'crazy' or 'hysterical' when confronted with relationship issues, particularly when it involves sexual betrayal. The use of the phrase 'fucking a goat' is intentionally crude and degrading, reinforcing the misogynistic trope that women are emotionally fragile and easily provoked by sexual infidelity. The overall intent is to ridicule and demean women by portraying them as irrational and overly emotional, fitting within the category of misogynous content.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_c7791d4a"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
